A||||6||DrkPicard||86 se v6 stalling too!||||8||
Z||000000||DrkPicard||08-17-2001||10:24 AM||||Id like to start off by saying hello im anew user here and thank you all for your help.<BR>I just picked up a 86 v6 se. got it for $0.<BR>the gut said it keeps fouling plugs. I ck'd it out found a bag egr valve (leak) replaced it no more vacume leak idles at about 900-1000 now. replaced plugs, cap, rtr, air, the usual tune up. Ck'd all other vacume lines look o.k.<BR>Started her up ran pretty good, every now and the you could feel a dead spot but was still pretty good. Now when its cold started it is o.k., if i let it idle for a while in park, the minute i step on the brake to shift into drive/reverse she stalls. i try to restart and she just cranks, i hold my foot to the floor she starts/skips etc.....then stalls back out??????<BR>the cat conv is new and not blocked. tune up parts new. any suggestions?????<BR>ps did get a ck eng light code for iac fluctuate over 50 ......||||reg||8
Z||000001||StuGood||08-17-2001||05:16 PM||||Kind of guessing here, but since you thanked us in advance...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Might start by replacing the ignition module with a new GM one, since they can fail due to exposure to heat.  If it isn't that, at least you have a replacement module to carry with you.  If the pickup coil in the distributor is at all questionable, replace it.  You have to pull the distributor out to replace this item.<P>I know you said you did the "usual tune up," so I apologize if you already did these.  Might also try cleaning out the idle air passage in the throttle body - if you're feeling ambitious, clean the whole thing.    <P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||DrkPicard||08-18-2001||10:38 AM||||i havent thought about the ignition module on it. I'll pick one up. I already did a full throttle body service on it as well......<BR>also tried to unplug the t/c sol switch, replaced the map sensor. It did run a lot better after doing that but when it is hot started it takes forever to start and runs with a skip/stumble condition, the stalling has gotten a bit better.....<P>p.s. just noticed all my typo's....anybody have white out??||||reg||1
Z||000003||roadwarrior||08-18-2001||12:36 PM||||just something else you might wanna check is your torque convertor and ignition timing||||reg||1
Z||000004||starfighter007@msn.com||08-18-2001||03:07 PM||||you may also want to check the brake booster as that is run by engine vacuam||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero651||08-19-2001||12:26 AM||||Now the only thing that sounds familiar to me was that it has a hard time starting when hot.  I had a problem for awhile that when I would shut off the car and than try to restart a couple minutes later it would not want to crank over.  I was told at the time that my starter was overheated because I was missing a heat sheild.  The starter failed eventually in a parking lot.  Just a suggestion take it for what it is worth.||||reg||1
Z||000006||DrkPicard||08-21-2001||01:17 AM||||Thanks to all for your input.<BR>At this point I have opted for pulling off the upper plenum...pulled fuel rail.<BR>ordered up a new regulator, and replacing o-rings on the injectors. Hope this helps. I also foun in the process corroded wire terminals at the coil capacator and also at the coolant switch so i'll repair this as well.<BR>I f I still have a problem I'll be looking for more info, wish me luck!||||reg||1
